<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses"><tei:p><tei:pb n="770" ed="1949 concluding_prayers" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n794_medium.jpg"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_34_10"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/34/10">Revere the Lord, you his holy ones; those who revere him suffer no want. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_34_11"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/34/11">Lions may be famishing and starving, but those who seek the Lord are not in want of any good thing. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_118_1"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/118/1">Give thanks to the Lord, for he is good; his mercy endures forever. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_145_16"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/145/16">Thou openest thy hand and satisfiest every living thing with favor. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/jeremiah_17_7"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/17/7">Blessed is the man who trusts in the Lord, ever relying on the Lord. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_37_25"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/37/25">I have been young and now I am old, but never have I seen the righteous man forsaken, nor his children begging bread. </tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:concluding_prayers/text/grace_verses/psalms_29_11"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/29/11">The Lord will give strength to his people; the Lord will bless his people with peace.</tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
